      "text": "299,308</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>.<|User|>Thank you for walking me through the steps. Can you also show me how to solve this problem using the distributive property of multiplication over addition?\n<think>\nCertainly! The distributive property of multiplication over addition states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. We can use this property to break down the multiplication of 864 and 806 into simpler parts. Let's rewrite 806 as 800 + 6 and then distribute 864 over this sum.\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can break down the multiplication of 864 and 806 as follows:\n\nFirst, we rewrite 806 as 800 + 6:\n```\n864 \u00d7 806 = 864 \u00d7 (800 + 6)\n```\n\nNext, we apply the distributive property:\n```\n864 \u00d7 (800 + 6) = 864 \u00d7 800 + 864 \u00d7 6\n```\n\nNow, we can calculate each term separately:\n```\n864 \u00d7 800 = 691,200\n864 \u00d7 6 = 4,184\n```\n\nFinally, we add the results of these two multiplications:\n```\n691,200 + 4,184 = 695,384\n```\n\nTherefore, the product of 864 and 806 is 695,384.\n</answer>",
